WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:04.553
A variable is a name that refers to a value You can
think of it

00:00:04.579 --> 00:00:09.921
as a clear label attached to a piece of information
For example the name sales

00:00:09.947 --> 00:00:15.958
can refer to the value one thousand while costs can
refer to eight hundred The

00:00:15.985 --> 00:00:20.221
assignment symbol tells Python to associate the name
on the left with the value on

00:00:20.248 --> 00:00:25.777
the right It is important not to think of assignment
exactly like an algebra equation

00:00:26.711 --> 00:00:32.708
In Python assignment means store this value under
this name Meaningful

00:00:32.721 --> 00:00:38.250
names make code easier to read A calculation such as
sales minus costs is

00:00:38.276 --> 00:00:43.789
immediately understandable A calculation using
unexplained numbers is much harder

00:00:43.816 --> 00:00:46.316
to maintain and much easier to misinterpret
